+## Required integrated artifact and isolated runtime addendum (2026-10-25)
+
+**Scope decision from the user:** ELMOS, HAVEN and KDAL are all required in the
+final thesis artifact. Optional-KDAL wording above is historical. Workspace
+instructions now state their required responsibilities while retaining the
+research/architecture and coordinated implementation gates. The moved baseline
+reference and affected navigation links have been repaired. This is not an
+approval to advance thesis stages or adopt runtime interfaces.
+
+The [integrated design package](../haven/docs/methodology/stage0/20261025-integration-design/README.md)
+proposes one CPU0 Linux guest with KDAL outside trusted EL2, ELMOS orchestration,
+and HAVEN admission. It includes observed/proposed architecture, seven boundary
+contracts, an end-to-end acceptance scenario, finding-specific prerequisites,
+M0–M5 and a concrete first coordinated artifact/preflight proposal. All remain
+review proposals; no coordinated implementation was applied.
+
+New observations:
+
+- KDAL's `kdal_attach_driver` invokes probe before assigning `device->driver`;
+  the static UART device has no association and `uart_probe` dereferences it.
+  Registry registration does not populate it first. This is a source-order
+  defect, not a recorded module-load failure. A separate KDAL lifecycle fix
+  and independent Linux functional baseline are required before integration.
+  The UAPI reports0.1.0; initial clients are AArch64 only because `compat_ioctl`
+  is absent. Invalid selection is name validation, not HAVEN authorization.
+- The local Linux6.6.80 source candidate exists outside the implementation
+  repositories, but has no `.config`, built Image, Module.symvers or generated
+  release header. No matching module exists in the inspected shared-module
+  directory. HAVEN still has no demonstrated Linux boot, guest DT/initramfs,
+  virtual GIC frontend or complete guest timer path. Bare-metal ERET and an LR
+  injection do not establish these capabilities. Source/config hashes and
+  missing inputs are recorded in the new package.
+- Authorized isolated runtime checks executed the unchanged memcpy proposal's
+  semantics fixture at EL2 with both default and diagnostic strict flags;
+  both passed and retained A's denial/resume marker. The exact preserved
+  aligned failure image reproduced, and the matched aligned source plus ABI
+  still faulted under default flags (ESR0x96000061, ELR0x800038ac, shifted
+  FAR0x8000701c). Its strict build passed the former checkpoint and existing
+  diagnostic SPI probe. These are five expected verdicts, including two
+  failure controls; no strict compiler flag or probe code was adopted.
+- External GDB hardware-breakpoint captures observe primary entry
+  SCTLR_EL2=0x30c50830 and primary post-init/fault0x30c51834, HCR0→0x80080039,
+  with TTBR0_EL2/TCR_EL2/MAIR_EL2 all0. Stage-1 M stays0 and A stays0 while
+  C/I are set by HAVEN. CPU2 before diagnostic init retains the entry state.
+  A1 is narrowed but remains open; A2 has new on-target evidence while its
+  tracked adoption remains gated. Full register/command/image/patch evidence
+  and the initial sandbox socket failure are preserved in the verified1,360-
+  file runtime archive outside ignored build directories.
+- For the minimum UP Linux slice, CPU2 startup and multicore CNTHP policy can
+  defer only after an explicit primary-only profile skips those paths. Guest
+  CNTV/PPI27 and bounded virtual interrupt delivery remain Linux prerequisites.
+  Physical GICD passthrough and generic skipped-fault handling are not accepted
+  shortcuts. The actual HAVEN negative is an excluded-page store with external
+  fault/canary evidence; a KDAL invalid-name errno is a separate API control.
+
+Revisions and existing implementation diffs are preserved. ELMOS and KDAL were
+inspected read-only. No Linux/KDAL integrated run, physical device, DMA or
+real-time behavior has been established. The next decision is review of CP1
+and its scoped prerequisites, not whether KDAL is included.
